machine|work-device|NOUN|Device that carries out work|A device that uses power to perform a task for people.|máy; thiết bị dùng năng lượng để thực hiện công việc|The machine cuts wooden boards into equal lengths.|Chiếc máy cắt các tấm ván thành những đoạn dài bằng nhau.|Machine is countable; a washing machine or sewing machine names a device by its task.|machine
traffic|road-vehicles|NOUN|Vehicles using roads|Vehicles moving along roads, considered together.|xe cộ lưu thông; giao thông đường bộ|Traffic slowed near the bridge while workers repaired the surface.|Xe cộ di chuyển chậm lại gần cầu trong lúc công nhân sửa mặt đường.|Traffic is uncountable; use heavy traffic for many vehicles and light traffic for relatively few.|traffic
spaceship|spacecraft|NOUN|Vehicle for space travel|A vehicle designed to travel beyond Earth's atmosphere into space.|tàu vũ trụ|The spaceship sent pictures of the planet back to Earth.|Tàu vũ trụ gửi hình ảnh của hành tinh về Trái Đất.|Spaceship is countable; it can describe a vehicle whether or not it carries people.|spaceship
bicycle|pedal-vehicle|NOUN|Two-wheeled pedal vehicle|A vehicle with two wheels that is moved by pushing pedals with the feet.|xe đạp|Nam locked his bicycle beside the community hall.|Nam khóa xe đạp của mình bên cạnh nhà sinh hoạt cộng đồng.|Bicycle is countable; ride a bicycle describes using it and by bicycle names the means of travel.|bicycle
dangerous|harm-risk|ADJECTIVE|Presenting a risk of harm|Likely to cause harm, injury or damage.|nguy hiểm; có nguy cơ gây hại|The broken ladder was too dangerous to use.|Chiếc thang bị hỏng quá nguy hiểm để sử dụng.|Use dangerous before a noun or after a linking verb; too dangerous to do describes an unacceptable risk.|dangerous
diploma|study-certificate|NOUN|Certificate of completed study|An official certificate showing that someone has completed a course of study.|bằng cấp; văn bằng xác nhận hoàn thành chương trình học|She displayed her diploma above the desk.|Cô ấy trưng bày văn bằng của mình phía trên bàn làm việc.|Diploma is countable; a diploma in a subject identifies the course, and it is not necessarily the same qualification as a degree.|diploma
month|calendar-period|NOUN|Division of a calendar year|One of the twelve periods into which a calendar year is divided.|tháng; một trong mười hai phần của năm theo lịch|The repairs should be finished by the end of next month.|Việc sửa chữa dự kiến hoàn tất trước khi tháng sau kết thúc.|Month is countable; next month needs no preposition, while once a month means one time in each month.|month
carry|support-and-move|VERB|Support while moving|Hold or support something while moving it from one place to another.|mang; cầm hoặc đỡ vật khi di chuyển|The porter carried our suitcases up the narrow stairs.|Người khuân hành lý mang những chiếc va li của chúng tôi lên cầu thang hẹp.|Carry takes a direct object; the past form is carried and the -ing form is carrying.|carry
jewel|precious-stone|NOUN|Valuable decorative stone|A valuable stone, often cut and polished for use in decoration.|đá quý; viên ngọc quý|A small jewel glittered in the silver ring.|Một viên đá quý nhỏ lấp lánh trên chiếc nhẫn bạc.|Jewel is countable; jewellery usually names ornaments collectively and is uncountable in British English.|jewel
cousin|aunt-uncle-child|NOUN|Child of an aunt or uncle|The child of your aunt or uncle.|anh, chị hoặc em họ; con của cô, dì, chú, bác hoặc cậu|My cousin helped me paint the wooden gate.|Người anh chị em họ của tôi giúp tôi sơn chiếc cổng gỗ.|Cousin does not specify gender or relative age; choose Vietnamese kinship terms according to context.|cousin
hotel|paid-lodging|NOUN|Place offering paid accommodation|A place where travellers can pay to stay in rooms for a short time.|khách sạn; nơi cung cấp phòng lưu trú có trả tiền|The hotel kept our luggage until the evening train.|Khách sạn giữ hành lý của chúng tôi cho đến giờ chuyến tàu tối.|Hotel is countable; stay at a hotel describes accommodation and book a hotel room describes reserving it.|hotel
main|principal|ADJECTIVE|Principal or most important|More important than the other related things, or serving as the principal one.|chính; chủ yếu|The main problem was a leak in the roof.|Vấn đề chính là một chỗ dột trên mái.|Main usually appears before a noun, such as main reason or main entrance; it normally does not take comparative forms.|main
olive|tree-fruit|NOUN|Small fruit of an olive tree|A small oval fruit, green or dark when prepared for eating, also used to make oil.|quả ô liu|She added sliced olives to the warm bread.|Cô ấy thêm ô liu thái lát vào bánh mì ấm.|Olive is countable when referring to the fruit; olive oil is an uncountable product made from it.|olive
ball|play-object|NOUN|Object used in play|A round or rounded object that people throw, kick or hit in a game.|quả bóng dùng để chơi|The ball rolled beneath the park bench.|Quả bóng lăn xuống dưới chiếc ghế dài trong công viên.|Ball is countable; the name of a sport can modify it, as in tennis ball or football.|ball
sing|vocal-music|VERB|Make music with the voice|Produce musical sounds with the voice, usually following a tune.|hát|The choir sang a quiet song at the end of the ceremony.|Dàn hợp xướng hát một bài nhẹ nhàng khi buổi lễ kết thúc.|The forms are sing, sang, sung; sing can stand alone or take a song as its object.|sing
volcano|eruptive-landform|NOUN|Opening that can release molten rock|An opening in Earth's surface, often forming a mountain, through which molten rock, ash and gases can escape.|núi lửa; nơi có thể phun dung nham, tro và khí|The village lies several kilometres from the volcano.|Ngôi làng nằm cách núi lửa vài ki lô mét.|Volcano is countable; volcanoes is a common plural, and an eruption names an event when material escapes.|volcano
taxi|hired-car|NOUN|Car hired with a driver|A car with a driver that passengers pay to take them to a destination.|xe taxi; ô tô có tài xế chở khách có trả tiền|We called a taxi when the rain became heavier.|Chúng tôi gọi một chiếc taxi khi mưa nặng hạt hơn.|Taxi is countable; take a taxi and travel by taxi describe transport, and cab is a common alternative name.|taxi
november|month-eleven|NOUN|Eleventh month|The eleventh month of the calendar year.|tháng Mười Một|The new library will open in November.|Thư viện mới sẽ mở cửa vào tháng Mười Một.|Write November with a capital N; use in November for the month and on with a specific date.|November
enclose|surround|VERB|Surround within a boundary|Surround something with a barrier or boundary so that it is contained inside.|bao quanh; rào quanh để giữ bên trong|A stone wall encloses the old orchard.|Một bức tường đá bao quanh vườn cây ăn quả cũ.|Enclose takes a direct object; be enclosed by identifies the surrounding barrier.|enclose
university|higher-education|NOUN|Institution for degree study|An educational institution where people study subjects at an advanced level and work towards degrees.|trường đại học|The university opened its laboratory to visiting schoolchildren.|Trường đại học mở phòng thí nghiệm cho học sinh đến tham quan.|University is countable; use a university because the initial sound is /j/, and at university commonly describes being a student.|university
